# feature-docs (Cursor adapter)

Note: current Cursor versions support the SKILL.md standard natively. Prefer
`./install.sh cursor` (installs to `~/.cursor/skills/`). Use this rule file only on older
Cursor versions, or as a repo-level nudge.

Copy this file into the target repo at `.cursor/rules/feature-docs.mdc` and replace
`<clone-path>` with where you cloned feature-init (for example `~/tools/feature-init`).

Full instructions, read and follow:
`<clone-path>/skills/feature-docs/SKILL.md`
(clone from https://github.com/codemeall/feature-init if missing)

Core rules:
- Specs and tickets live in `.scratch/<feature>/` (local, untracked). The tracked record of a
  built feature is `docs/<feature>/feature-docs/`: overview.md, decisions.md, tickets.md,
  sources.json.
- Before speccing or changing a feature, read its decisions.md and cite the decision IDs the
  change builds on or overturns.
- After implementation, write the feature docs from the spec, the tickets and the code. Every
  "What was built" row cites a real file; work the code does not show is "Not built yet".
- When `.scratch/<feature>/` changes, run
  `bash <clone-path>/skills/feature-docs/scripts/feature-docs.sh status .` and update the rows
  for the files it names, then `stamp`.
- Superseded decisions and withdrawn tickets keep their rows.
